list, it does seem archaic. I also see it as possible to interact with a
phpBB forum as though it were a mailing list: it could mail out posts to
people who choose this method of interaction and those people could mail
their posts to the board. (this likely will take tweaking of the phpBB code
to do effectively, I'm not sure) I keep mentioning phpBB because the extant
lojban web boards use this software (it's good software, too IMHO).

adam
           
